## Native Agentic

The PyFly dependency is pinned to the official release wheel matching the CLI
version that generated this project. If that CLI came from an unreleased source
checkout, publish its matching release wheel before running `uv sync`.

Agentic is enabled explicitly in `pyfly.yaml`. Inject `AgentFactory` from
`pyfly.agentic.factory` into services to create application-owned agents.
Pass a model explicitly or set `pyfly.agentic.default_model` before running an
agent. Keep provider credentials in environment variables. For offline tests,
pass `pydantic_ai.models.test.TestModel()`; no provider credentials are needed.

Storage and integration extras are separate choices. Add the `agentic-` extras
your application needs to its PyFly dependency, retaining any release wheel URL.
In existing projects, `pyfly add agentic` preserves direct references and pins
unversioned requirements to the CLI version's official wheel. A version constraint
without a direct reference requires explicitly selecting a compatible wheel first.
See the [Agentic guide](https://fireflyframework.github.io/fireflyframework-pyfly/docs/modules/agentic/)
for configuration.

